Dialogue: 0,0:00:00.00,0:00:03.91,Default,,0,0,0,,Welcome back to DevTalk English, everyone!\N{\c&H00E1A62B&}/ˈwɛlkəm ˈbæk tə ˈdɛvˌtɔk ˈɪŋɡlɪʃ ˈɛvriˌwʌn/
Dialogue: 0,0:00:03.91,0:00:10.74,Default,,0,0,0,,Today, we're diving into why I started my channel in English, despite\Nnot being fluent.\N{\c&H00E1A62B&}/təˈdeɪ wɪr ˈdaɪvɪŋ ˈɪntu waɪ aɪ ˈstɑrtəd maɪ ˈtʃænəl ɪn ˈɪŋɡlɪʃ\Ndɪˈspaɪt nɑt ˈbiɪŋ ˈfluənt/
Dialogue: 0,0:00:10.74,0:00:16.01,Default,,0,0,0,,You know, it all began with my first job interview in English.\N{\c&H00E1A62B&}/ju noʊ ɪt ɔl bɪˈɡæn wɪð maɪ fɜrst dʒɑb ˈɪntərˌvju ɪn ˈɪŋɡlɪʃ/
Dialogue: 0,0:00:16.01,0:00:21.15,Default,,0,0,0,,I was super nervous. I mixed up 'bug' and 'feature' like three times.\N{\c&H00E1A62B&}/aɪ wəz ˈsupər ˈnɜrvəs aɪ mɪkst ʌp bʌɡ ənd ˈfitʃər laɪk θri taɪmz/
Dialogue: 0,0:00:21.15,0:00:26.04,Default,,0,0,0,,And let me tell you, my interviewer was not impressed.\N{\c&H00E1A62B&}/ənd lɛt mi tɛl ju maɪ ˈɪntərˌvjuər wəz nɑt ɪmˈprɛst/
Dialogue: 0,0:00:26.04,0:00:29.99,Default,,0,0,0,,Oh no, sounds tough! What happened then?\N{\c&H00E1A62B&}/oʊ noʊ saʊndz tʌf wʌt ˈhæpənd ðɛn/
Dialogue: 0,0:00:29.99,0:00:35.82,Default,,0,0,0,,Well, I didn't get the job, but it got me thinking about my\Nlanguage skills.\N{\c&H00E1A62B&}/wɛl aɪ ˈdɪdənt ɡɛt ðə dʒɑb bət ɪt ɡɑt mi ˈθɪŋkɪŋ əˈbaʊt maɪ\Nˈlæŋɡwɪdʒ skɪlz/
Dialogue: 0,0:00:35.82,0:00:41.62,Default,,0,0,0,,I realized I had to improve, but I didn't want to wait until I\Nwas perfect.\N{\c&H00E1A62B&}/aɪ ˈriəˌlaɪzd aɪ hæd tə ɪmˈpruv bət aɪ ˈdɪdənt wɑnt tə weɪt ənˈtɪl aɪ\Nwəz ˈpɜrfɪkt/
Dialogue: 0,0:00:41.62,0:00:47.19,Default,,0,0,0,,So I thought, why not start sharing my coding journey in English?\N{\c&H00E1A62B&}/soʊ aɪ θɔt waɪ nɑt stɑrt ˈʃɛrɪŋ maɪ ˈkoʊdɪŋ ˈdʒɜrni ɪn ˈɪŋɡlɪʃ/
Dialogue: 0,0:00:47.19,0:00:50.54,Default,,0,0,0,,And did you find any surprising benefits?\N{\c&H00E1A62B&}/ənd dɪd ju faɪnd ˈɛni səˈpraɪzɪŋ ˈbɛnəfɪts/
Dialogue: 0,0:00:50.54,0:00:58.03,Default,,0,0,0,,Absolutely, Mia. Embracing my imperfect English led to\Nunexpected opportunities.\N{\c&H00E1A62B&}/ˈæbsəˌlutli ˈmiə ɛmˈbreɪsɪŋ maɪ ɪmˈpɜrfɪkt ˈɪŋɡlɪʃ lɛd tə\Nˌʌnɪkˈspɛktɪd ˌɑpərˈtunətiz/
Dialogue: 0,0:00:58.03,0:01:05.28,Default,,0,0,0,,I remember this one project where I struggled with an API because all\Ndocs were in English.\N{\c&H00E1A62B&}/aɪ rɪˈmɛmbər ðɪs wʌn ˈprɑdʒɛkt wɛr aɪ ˈstrʌɡəld wɪð ən ˌeɪˈpiˌaɪ\Nbɪˈkəz ɔl dɑks wɜr ɪn ˈɪŋɡlɪʃ/
Dialogue: 0,0:01:05.28,0:01:12.95,Default,,0,0,0,,I spent hours just trying to understand basic usage instructions and\Nstill missed deadlines.\N{\c&H00E1A62B&}/aɪ spɛnt ˈaʊərz dʒəst ˈtraɪɪŋ tə ˌʌndərˈstænd ˈbeɪsɪk ˈjusɪdʒ\Nɪnˈstrʌkʃənz ənd stɪl mɪst ˈdɛdˌlaɪnz/
Dialogue: 0,0:01:12.95,0:01:20.94,Default,,0,0,0,,That frustration was a turning point. I knew I couldn't be alone in\Nfeeling lost with English resources.\N{\c&H00E1A62B&}/ðæt frəˈstreɪʃən wəz ə ˈtɜrnɪŋ pɔɪnt aɪ nu aɪ ˈkʊdənt bi əˈloʊn ɪn\Nˈfilɪŋ lɔst wɪð ˈɪŋɡlɪʃ ˈrisɔrsɪz/
Dialogue: 0,0:01:20.94,0:01:23.86,Default,,0,0,0,,Wow, so you felt a real gap there?\N{\c&H00E1A62B&}/waʊ soʊ ju fɛlt ə ril ɡæp ðɛr/
Dialogue: 0,0:01:23.86,0:01:32.84,Default,,0,0,0,,Yes, exactly! There were so few resources for developers learning in\NEnglish as a second language.\N{\c&H00E1A62B&}/jɛs ɪɡˈzæktli ðɛr wɜr soʊ fju ˈrisɔrsɪz fər dɪˈvɛləpərz ˈlɜrnɪŋ ɪn\Nˈɪŋɡlɪʃ əz ə ˈsɛkənd ˈlæŋɡwɪdʒ/
Dialogue: 0,0:01:32.84,0:01:38.46,Default,,0,0,0,,I thought, 'If I’m struggling, others must be too.' It was a\Nlightbulb moment.\N{\c&H00E1A62B&}/aɪ θɔt ɪf aɪm ˈstrʌɡəlɪŋ ˈʌðərz məst bi tu ɪt wəz ə\Nˈlaɪtˌbʌlb ˈmoʊmənt/
Dialogue: 0,0:01:38.46,0:01:41.44,Default,,0,0,0,,So you wanted to help others like you?\N{\c&H00E1A62B&}/soʊ ju ˈwɑntɪd tə hɛlp ˈʌðərz laɪk ju/
Dialogue: 0,0:01:41.44,0:01:49.38,Default,,0,0,0,,Yes, totally. I wanted to create something for developers who feel\Nleft out due to language barriers.\N{\c&H00E1A62B&}/jɛs ˈtoʊtəli aɪ ˈwɑntɪd tə kriˈeɪt ˈsʌmθɪŋ fər dɪˈvɛləpərz hu fil\Nlɛft aʊt du tə ˈlæŋɡwɪdʒ ˈbɛriərz/
Dialogue: 0,0:01:49.38,0:01:55.91,Default,,0,0,0,,I remember one friend who almost gave up coding because of\NEnglish documentation.\N{\c&H00E1A62B&}/aɪ rɪˈmɛmbər wʌn frɛnd hu ˈɔlmoʊst ɡeɪv ʌp ˈkoʊdɪŋ bɪˈkəz əv\Nˈɪŋɡlɪʃ ˌdɑkjəˌmɛnˈteɪʃən/
Dialogue: 0,0:01:55.91,0:02:02.16,Default,,0,0,0,,He was such a talented developer, but the language kept blocking\Nhis progress.\N{\c&H00E1A62B&}/hi wəz sʌtʃ ə ˈtæləntəd dɪˈvɛləpər bət ðə ˈlæŋɡwɪdʒ kɛpt ˈblɑkɪŋ\Nhɪz ˈprɑɡrɛs/
Dialogue: 0,0:02:02.16,0:02:05.41,Default,,0,0,0,,That must have been frustrating for him.\N{\c&H00E1A62B&}/ðæt məst əv bɪn ˈfrəˌstreɪtɪŋ fər hɪm/
Dialogue: 0,0:02:05.41,0:02:12.99,Default,,0,0,0,,Exactly. Watching him struggle made me realize the urgency of creating\Naccessible content.\N{\c&H00E1A62B&}/ɪɡˈzæktli ˈwɑtʃɪŋ hɪm ˈstrʌɡəl meɪd mi ˈriəˌlaɪz ði ˈɜrdʒənsi əv\Nkriˈeɪtɪŋ ækˈsɛsəbəl ˈkɑntɛnt/
Dialogue: 0,0:02:12.99,0:02:19.87,Default,,0,0,0,,So I decided to just go for it, imperfections and all, and start\Nmy channel.\N{\c&H00E1A62B&}/soʊ aɪ dəˈsaɪdəd tə dʒəst ɡoʊ fər ɪt ˌɪmpərˈfɛkʃənz ənd ɔl ənd stɑrt\Nmaɪ ˈtʃænəl/
Dialogue: 0,0:02:19.87,0:02:25.15,Default,,0,0,0,,And now you're reaching so many developers. That's amazing, Alex!\N{\c&H00E1A62B&}/ənd naʊ jʊr ˈritʃɪŋ soʊ ˈmɛni dɪˈvɛləpərz ðæts əˈmeɪzɪŋ ˈæləks/
Dialogue: 0,0:02:25.15,0:02:30.22,Default,,0,0,0,,But honestly, I was terrified of the criticism at first.\N{\c&H00E1A62B&}/bət ˈɑnəstli aɪ wəz ˈtɛrəˌfaɪd əv ðə ˈkrɪtɪˌsɪzəm ət fɜrst/
Dialogue: 0,0:02:30.22,0:02:32.41,Default,,0,0,0,,What did people say?\N{\c&H00E1A62B&}/wət dɪd ˈpipəl seɪ/
Dialogue: 0,0:02:32.41,0:02:37.58,Default,,0,0,0,,Most comments were supportive, but one viewer really got to me.\N{\c&H00E1A62B&}/moʊst ˈkɑmɛnts wɜr səˈpɔrtɪv bət wʌn ˈvjuər ˈrɪli ɡɑt tə mi/
Dialogue: 0,0:02:37.58,0:02:42.21,Default,,0,0,0,,They said my accent made my tutorials hard to follow.\N{\c&H00E1A62B&}/ðeɪ sɛd maɪ ˈæksɛnt meɪd maɪ tuˈtɔriəlz hɑrd tə ˈfɑloʊ/
Dialogue: 0,0:02:42.21,0:02:46.05,Default,,0,0,0,,I almost hit delete on everything right then.\N{\c&H00E1A62B&}/aɪ ˈɔlmoʊst hɪt dɪˈlit ɑn ˈɛvriˌθɪŋ raɪt ðɛn/
Dialogue: 0,0:02:46.05,0:02:48.57,Default,,0,0,0,,Wow, that must have hurt.\N{\c&H00E1A62B&}/waʊ ðæt məst əv hɜrt/
Dialogue: 0,0:02:48.57,0:02:53.61,Default,,0,0,0,,It did, but I realized I needed to focus on the positives.\N{\c&H00E1A62B&}/ɪt dɪd bət aɪ ˈriəˌlaɪzd aɪ ˈnidəd tə ˈfoʊkəs ɑn ðə ˈpɑzətɪvz/
Dialogue: 0,0:02:53.61,0:02:58.50,Default,,0,0,0,,Other viewers commented about how my content was helpful.\N{\c&H00E1A62B&}/ˈʌðər ˈvjuərz ˈkɑmɛntəd əˈbaʊt haʊ maɪ ˈkɑntɛnt wəz ˈhɛlpfəl/
Dialogue: 0,0:02:58.50,0:03:03.35,Default,,0,0,0,,One even said my mistakes made them feel more at ease.\N{\c&H00E1A62B&}/wʌn ˈivɪn sɛd maɪ məˈsteɪks meɪd ðɛm fil mɔr æt iz/
Dialogue: 0,0:03:03.35,0:03:07.87,Default,,0,0,0,,That's really nice. Mistakes are part of learning, right?\N{\c&H00E1A62B&}/ðæts ˈrɪli naɪs məˈsteɪks ɑr pɑrt əv ˈlɜrnɪŋ raɪt/
Dialogue: 0,0:03:07.87,0:03:13.83,Default,,0,0,0,,Exactly! I decided to embrace the learning curve publicly.\N{\c&H00E1A62B&}/ɪɡˈzæktli aɪ dɪˈsaɪdəd tu ɛmˈbreɪs ðə ˈlɜrnɪŋ kɜrv ˈpʌblɪkli/
Dialogue: 0,0:03:13.83,0:03:18.95,Default,,0,0,0,,Facing those fears has actually improved my English a lot.\N{\c&H00E1A62B&}/ˈfeɪsɪŋ ðoʊz fɪrz hæz ˈækʧuəli ɪmˈpruvd maɪ ˈɪŋɡlɪʃ ə lɑt/
Dialogue: 0,0:03:18.95,0:03:24.63,Default,,0,0,0,,Now, I'm more confident even when I deploy code or do a code review.\N{\c&H00E1A62B&}/naʊ aɪm mɔr ˈkɑnfədənt ˈivɪn wɛn aɪ dɪˈplɔɪ koʊd ɔr du ə koʊd rɪˈvju/
Dialogue: 0,0:03:24.63,0:03:29.07,Default,,0,0,0,,That's so encouraging. You've come a long way, Alex!\N{\c&H00E1A62B&}/ðæts soʊ ɪnˈkɜrɪʤɪŋ juv kʌm ə lɔŋ weɪ ˈæləks/
Dialogue: 0,0:03:29.07,0:03:33.75,Default,,0,0,0,,Wow, it seems like the support really changed things for you.\N{\c&H00E1A62B&}/waʊ ɪt simz laɪk ðə səˈpɔrt ˈrɪli ʧeɪndʒd θɪŋz fɔr ju/
Dialogue: 0,0:03:33.75,0:03:41.03,Default,,0,0,0,,Yeah, it was a big turning point. I realized people valued\Nauthenticity over perfection.\N{\c&H00E1A62B&}/jæ ɪt wəz ə bɪɡ ˈtɜrnɪŋ pɔɪnt aɪ ˈriəˌlaɪzd ˈpipəl ˈvæljud\Nɔˌθɛnˈtɪsɪti ˈoʊvər pərˈfɛkʃən/
Dialogue: 0,0:03:41.03,0:03:48.24,Default,,0,0,0,,Once, I posted a video with a bug in my code, and instead of\Ncriticism, I got help.\N{\c&H00E1A62B&}/wʌns aɪ ˈpoʊstəd ə ˈvɪdioʊ wɪð ə bʌɡ ɪn maɪ koʊd ənd ɪnˈstɛd əv\Nˈkrɪtɪˌsɪzəm aɪ ɡɑt hɛlp/
Dialogue: 0,0:03:48.24,0:03:55.87,Default,,0,0,0,,Viewers suggested solutions and shared similar experiences. It felt\Nlike a team effort.\N{\c&H00E1A62B&}/ˈvjuərz səˈʤɛstəd səˈluʃənz ənd ʃɛrd ˈsɪmələr ɪkˈspɪriənsɪz ɪt fɛlt\Nlaɪk ə tim ˈɛfərt/
Dialogue: 0,0:03:55.87,0:04:01.45,Default,,0,0,0,,That's amazing! Your mistakes actually brought people together.\N{\c&H00E1A62B&}/ðæts əˈmeɪzɪŋ jʊr məˈsteɪks ˈækʧuəli brɔt ˈpipəl təˈɡɛðər/
Dialogue: 0,0:04:01.45,0:04:08.21,Default,,0,0,0,,Exactly. It was like forming a community around learning and\Ngrowing together.\N{\c&H00E1A62B&}/ɪɡˈzæktli ɪt wəz laɪk ˈfɔrmɪŋ ə kəˈmjunɪti əˈraʊnd ˈlɜrnɪŋ ənd\Nˈɡroʊɪŋ təˈɡɛðər/
Dialogue: 0,0:04:08.21,0:04:14.57,Default,,0,0,0,,This support made me more confident in other areas, like presenting\Nnew APIs.\N{\c&H00E1A62B&}/ðɪs səˈpɔrt meɪd mi mɔr ˈkɑnfədənt ɪn ˈʌðər ˈɛriəz laɪk prɪˈzɛntɪŋ\Nnu ˌeɪˌpiˈaɪz/
Dialogue: 0,0:04:14.57,0:04:20.63,Default,,0,0,0,,Before, I would overthink every word, but now I focus more on\Nthe message.\N{\c&H00E1A62B&}/bɪˈfɔr aɪ wəd ˌoʊvərˈθɪŋk ˈɛvri wɜrd bət naʊ aɪ ˈfoʊkəs mɔr ɑn\Nðə ˈmɛsɪʤ/
Dialogue: 0,0:04:20.63,0:04:25.76,Default,,0,0,0,,Your focus shifted from language to connection. That’s powerful!\N{\c&H00E1A62B&}/jʊr ˈfoʊkəs ˈʃɪftəd frəm ˈlæŋɡwɪʤ tə kəˈnɛkʃən ðæts ˈpaʊərfəl/
Dialogue: 0,0:04:25.76,0:04:32.07,Default,,0,0,0,,Yes, exactly. People connecting over code, even with\Nlanguage barriers.\N{\c&H00E1A62B&}/jɛs ɪɡˈzæktli ˈpipəl kəˈnɛktɪŋ ˈoʊvər koʊd ˈivɪn wɪð\Nˈlæŋɡwɪʤ ˈbɛriərz/
Dialogue: 0,0:04:32.07,0:04:38.02,Default,,0,0,0,,One viewer said seeing my struggles made them feel less alone\Nin theirs.\N{\c&H00E1A62B&}/wʌn ˈvjuər sɛd ˈsiɪŋ maɪ ˈstrʌɡəlz meɪd ðɛm fil lɛs əˈloʊn ɪn ðɛrz/
Dialogue: 0,0:04:38.02,0:04:42.44,Default,,0,0,0,,That’s when I knew my channel was making a real impact.\N{\c&H00E1A62B&}/ðæts wɛn aɪ nu maɪ ˈtʃænəl wəz ˈmeɪkɪŋ ə ˈril ˈɪmpækt/
Dialogue: 0,0:04:42.44,0:04:47.43,Default,,0,0,0,,And you've inspired so many others to start despite imperfections.\N{\c&H00E1A62B&}/ænd juv ɪnˈspaɪrd soʊ ˈmɛni ˈʌðərz tə stɑrt dɪˈspaɪt ˌɪmpərˈfɛkʃənz/
Dialogue: 0,0:04:47.43,0:04:53.13,Default,,0,0,0,,Thanks, Mia. It's been a journey, but I'm grateful for every step.\N{\c&H00E1A62B&}/θæŋks ˈmiə ɪts bɪn ə ˈdʒɜrni bət aɪm ˈɡreɪtfəl fɔr ˈɛvri stɛp/
Dialogue: 0,0:04:53.13,0:04:58.22,Default,,0,0,0,,So you turned your limits into strengths and stayed true to yourself.\N{\c&H00E1A62B&}/soʊ ju tɜrnd jʊr ˈlɪməts ˈɪntu strɛŋkθs ənd steɪd tru tə jʊrˈsɛlf/
Dialogue: 0,0:04:58.22,0:05:05.34,Default,,0,0,0,,Exactly! Authenticity became my strength, and it resonated with\Nso many.\N{\c&H00E1A62B&}/ɪɡˈzæktli ɔˈθɛntɪˈsɪti bɪˈkeɪm maɪ strɛŋkθ ənd ɪt ˈrɛzəˌneɪtɪd wɪð\Nsoʊ ˈmɛni/
Dialogue: 0,0:05:05.34,0:05:10.50,Default,,0,0,0,,It's all about showing up as you are and connecting genuinely.\N{\c&H00E1A62B&}/ɪts ɔl əˈbaʊt ˈʃoʊɪŋ ʌp əz ju ɑr ənd kəˈnɛktɪŋ ˈdʒɛnjʊɪnli/
Dialogue: 0,0:05:10.50,0:05:14.25,Default,,0,0,0,,That's such a refreshing perspective, Alex.\N{\c&H00E1A62B&}/ðæts sʌtʃ ə rəˈfrɛʃɪŋ pərˈspɛktɪv ˈæləks/
Dialogue: 0,0:05:14.25,0:05:20.67,Default,,0,0,0,,Thanks, Mia. I want to encourage our listeners to start projects\Nthey fear.\N{\c&H00E1A62B&}/θæŋks ˈmiə aɪ wɑnt tʊ ɪnˈkɜrɪdʒ aʊər ˈlɪsənərz tə stɑrt ˈprɑdʒɛkts\Nðeɪ fɪr/
Dialogue: 0,0:05:20.67,0:05:26.26,Default,,0,0,0,,Try that new API or share your code — even if you're scared at first.\N{\c&H00E1A62B&}/traɪ ðæt nu ˈeɪˈpiˈaɪ ɔr ʃɛr jʊr koʊd ivɪn ɪf jʊr skɛrd æt fɜrst/
Dialogue: 0,0:05:26.26,0:05:31.44,Default,,0,0,0,,It's the learning process that truly matters, not perfection.\N{\c&H00E1A62B&}/ɪts ðə ˈlɜrnɪŋ ˈprɑsɛs ðæt ˈtruli ˈmætərz nɑt pərˈfɛkʃən/
Dialogue: 0,0:05:31.44,0:05:35.61,Default,,0,0,0,,And every developer's voice is unique and brings value.\N{\c&H00E1A62B&}/ænd ˈɛvri dɪˈvɛləpərz vɔɪs ɪz juˈnik ənd brɪŋz ˈvælju/
Dialogue: 0,0:05:35.61,0:05:39.83,Default,,0,0,0,,Don't let language hold you back from sharing your ideas.\N{\c&H00E1A62B&}/doʊnt lɛt ˈlæŋɡwɪdʒ hoʊld ju bæk frəm ˈʃɛrɪŋ jʊr aɪˈdiəz/
Dialogue: 0,0:05:39.83,0:05:44.79,Default,,0,0,0,,Absolutely. Let's keep pushing boundaries together!\N{\c&H00E1A62B&}/ˈæbsəˌlutli lɛts kip ˈpʊʃɪŋ ˈbaʊndriz təˈɡɛðər/
Dialogue: 0,0:05:44.79,0:05:50.58,Default,,0,0,0,,I remember the first video I posted; it was about\Ndebugging JavaScript.\N{\c&H00E1A62B&}/aɪ rɪˈmɛmbər ðə fɜrst ˈvɪdioʊ aɪ ˈpoʊstəd ɪt wəz əˈbaʊt\Ndɪˈbʌɡɪŋ ˈdʒævəˌskrɪpt/
Dialogue: 0,0:05:50.58,0:05:55.51,Default,,0,0,0,,My accent was heavy, and I stumbled over some words.\N{\c&H00E1A62B&}/maɪ ˈæksɛnt wəz ˈhɛvi ənd aɪ ˈstʌmbəld ˈoʊvər səm wɜrdz/
Dialogue: 0,0:05:55.51,0:05:59.60,Default,,0,0,0,,But the comments were surprisingly supportive!\N{\c&H00E1A62B&}/bət ðə ˈkɑmənts wɜr sərˈpraɪzɪŋli səˈpɔrtɪv/
Dialogue: 0,0:05:59.60,0:06:02.66,Default,,0,0,0,,Really? Viewers were nice?\N{\c&H00E1A62B&}/ˈrɪli ˈvjuərz wɜr naɪs/
Dialogue: 0,0:06:02.66,0:06:07.43,Default,,0,0,0,,Yeah, they appreciated the content and even offered tips.\N{\c&H00E1A62B&}/jæ ðeɪ əˈpriʃieɪtɪd ðə ˈkɑntɛnt ənd ˈivɪn ˈɔfərd tɪps/
Dialogue: 0,0:06:07.43,0:06:11.97,Default,,0,0,0,,It was like having an unexpected team cheering for me.\N{\c&H00E1A62B&}/ɪt wəz laɪk ˈhævɪŋ ən ˌʌnɪkˈspɛktɪd tim ˈtʃɪrɪŋ fɔr mi/
Dialogue: 0,0:06:11.97,0:06:14.64,Default,,0,0,0,,That must've felt amazing!\N{\c&H00E1A62B&}/ðæt ˈmʌstəv fɛlt əˈmeɪzɪŋ/
Dialogue: 0,0:06:14.64,0:06:19.58,Default,,0,0,0,,It did, and it motivated me to keep uploading regularly.\N{\c&H00E1A62B&}/ɪt dɪd ənd ɪt ˈmoʊtəˌveɪtəd mi tə kip ˈʌpˌloʊdɪŋ ˈrɛɡjələrli/
Dialogue: 0,0:06:19.58,0:06:25.73,Default,,0,0,0,,Each video, I noticed small improvements in my English and confidence.\N{\c&H00E1A62B&}/itʃ ˈvɪdioʊ aɪ ˈnoʊtɪst smɔl ɪmˈpruvmənts ɪn maɪ ˈɪŋɡlɪʃ\Nənd ˈkɑnfədəns/
Dialogue: 0,0:06:25.73,0:06:31.21,Default,,0,0,0,,So it was a win-win: improving skills and sharing knowledge!\N{\c&H00E1A62B&}/soʊ ɪt wəz ə ˈwɪnˌwɪn ɪmˈpruvɪŋ skɪlz ənd ˈʃɛrɪŋ ˈnɑlɪdʒ/
Dialogue: 0,0:06:31.21,0:06:36.86,Default,,0,0,0,,Thanks for listening to this episode of DevTalk English. See you\Nnext time!\N{\c&H00E1A62B&}/θæŋks fɔr ˈlɪsənɪŋ tə ðɪs ˈɛpəˌsoʊd əv ˈdɛvˌtɔk ˈɪŋɡlɪʃ si ju\Nnɛkst taɪm/
